# Lesson 5: Fixing code: errors, quick fixes, rename, format

The practice project has three deliberate mistakes. Fix them all using only
the keys in this lesson. Start fresh: `:Practice`{vim}  (`]t`{normal} / `[t`{normal} to switch)

# 5.1 Find the errors

  `]d`{normal} / `[d`{normal}   next / previous problem (error, warning or hint)
  `]D`{normal} / `[D`{normal}   last / first problem in the file
  `gl`{normal}         show the full message for the problem under the cursor

Errors are underlined, marked in the left column and summarised at the end
of the line.

 1. Open src/cart.ts. Press `]d`{normal}: you land on `Money`, underlined in red.
 2. Press `gl`{normal}: "Cannot find name 'Money'". It's used but never imported.

# 5.2 Quick fixes: code actions

  `<Space>la`{normal}   code actions for the cursor position: fixes, imports, refactors
  `<Space>lA`{normal}   source actions for the whole file (organise imports, fix all)

 1. With the cursor on `Money`, press `<Space>la`{normal}.
 2. Choose the action that adds or updates the import from "./money".
    Line 1 becomes `import { addMoney, Money } from "./money";` (or similar),
    and every `Money` error in the file disappears.

Code actions are worth trying on ANY error: missing imports, unused variables,
"add missing property", converting functions and more, depending on the language.

# 5.3 Rename everywhere

  `<Space>lr`{normal}   rename the symbol under the cursor, in every file that uses it

The method `totl` in cart.ts is misspelled, and index.ts calls it.

 1. In cart.ts, put the cursor on `totl` and press `<Space>lr`{normal}.
 2. Type `total` and press `<Enter>`{normal}.
 3. Open index.ts (`<Space>fs`{normal}): its call became `cart.total()` too.

Never search-and-replace a name by hand again: rename understands scope, so it
won't touch an unrelated `totl` somewhere else.

# 5.4 The last error, by hand

 1. In index.ts, press `]d`{normal} to reach the error on the second `cart.add`.
 2. `gl`{normal}: "Type 'string' is not assignable to type 'number'".
 3. Remove the quotes around "1" (a quantity is a number, not text): search for
    it with `/"1"`{normal} `<Enter>`{normal} (the cursor lands on the opening quote), then
    `x`{normal} deletes that quote, `l`{normal} steps onto the closing one, `x`{normal} deletes it.
 4. The error disappears a moment later.

# 5.5 Formatting

Files are formatted automatically when you save (`<Space>w`{normal}).
  `<Space>lf`{normal}   format now
  `<Space>uf`{normal}   turn format-on-save off / on for this buffer (`<Space>uF`{normal} for all)

 1. In money.ts, mess up the indentation of a few lines (`>>`{normal} indents a line).
 2. `<Space>lf`{normal}: back to tidy.

# 5.6 The problems list, and TODOs

  `<Space>xx`{normal}   problems in this file, as a list (Trouble)
  `<Space>xX`{normal}   problems in the whole project
  `<Space>xt`{normal}   every TODO / FIXME comment in the project
  `<Space>lD`{normal}   search problems with the picker

In the list: `j`{normal}/`k`{normal} to move, `<Enter>`{normal} to jump to it, `q`{normal} to close.

 1. Run `:Practice`{vim} again to get all the errors back, then `<Space>xX`{normal}.
    Both files' errors in one list. Fix them from there.
 2. `<Space>xt`{normal}: the TODO in cart.ts shows up. `<Enter>`{normal} on it.

# 5.7 Quieter or louder

  `<Space>ud`{normal}   hide / show diagnostics (when you're mid-refactor and the red is noise)

# Recap

  next problem  `]d`   read it  `gl`   quick fix  `<Space>la`   rename  `<Space>lr`
  format  `<Space>lf`   problems list  `<Space>xx` / `<Space>xX`   TODOs  `<Space>xt`

Next: `:Tutor my-06-git-tasks`{vim}
